  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe report: Stepover from 3 mm to 25 mm left the path unchanged. The path was correct. Adaptive and Offset rings step by **Optimal load** (`load_step(D, optimal_load)`) and never read Stepover. Zigzag, Waterline and Auto space their rows by Stepover. The Passes tab showed both fields for every strategy, so one of them was always dead.\n\n- `PocketStrategy::steps_by_load()` (motion) names the load strategies. `tiling_step` in the 2D and 3D pocket params now uses it, and so does every page guard. One predicate covers both the generator and the page.\n- **Passes tab** (Pocket, 3D Pocket, Rotary offset, Multi-axis rough): Stepover shows only for Zigzag, Waterline and Auto. Optimal load shows only for Adaptive and Offset rings. The 2D Adaptive kind no longer shows Stepover; 2D Offset keeps it.\n- Every Optimal load field has a hint: \"this load sets the step between passes - Stepover is not used here (it spaces Zigzag, Waterline and Auto)\".\n- **Leads tab, Engagement**: a hint says it changes the entry feeds only, and that the side load of the passes is Stepover or Optimal load on Passes. This answers the \"which is actually winning\" question.\n- **Trochoid**: a hint says Forward step is the most a loop advances, and that the loops shorten where Max engagement would be exceeded.\n- **3D validate**: a stepover wider than the tool is refused only for strategies that read it. Before, a stale value refused a legal Adaptive job. A stepover of zero or less is still refused for every strategy.\n- **2D past-reach refusal** now names the field (\"stepover\" / \"optimal-load step\") and both values.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1512-stepover-load.md` (hide the inert field rather than make Adaptive read Stepover; Engagement group name kept).\n\nNo change to posted G-code, goldens, the project file or commands. MCP: no new command; the parameters were already settable.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `crates/motion/tests/radial_step.rs`:\n  - `zigzag_rows_follow_the_stepover`\n  - `a_stepover_past_reach_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `load_strategies_step_by_the_load_not_the_stepover`: Offset rings with stepover 3 vs 25 gives identical moves; load 0.10 vs 0.30 differs\n  - `adaptive_clearing_never_reads_the_stepover`\n  - `steps_by_load_names_the_load_strategies`\n  - `pocket3d_offset_rings_ignore_a_stale_wide_stepover`\n- `crates/motion/tests/machining3d.rs` `adaptive_refuses_what_the_law_refuses`: updated. Adaptive with stepover 9 > D now validates; Zigzag with stepover 9 is refused; stepover 0 is refused.\n- UI, structural: new `egui_app::tests::radial_step_field::the_pocket_passes_tab_shows_only_the_step_its_strategy_reads`. In `every_field_lives_on_exactly_one_section`, the 2D Adaptive Passes row drops \"Stepover\".\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green: motion, app and ui suites, 0 failed (9.6 min wall)\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI by hand (no screenshots: hidden rows and hint lines only, no layout change).\n- The Passes rows of the rotary offset and multi-axis rough pages under the load strategies (their defaults are non-load, so the structural table covers only the default rows).\n- Release heavy lanes and pixel snapshots (no PNG touched).\n\nChangelog: Passes page shows one radial-step field per strategy: Stepover for Zigzag/Waterline/Auto, Optimal load for Adaptive/Offset rings; entry Engagement and trochoid step say what they change (#1512)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1512\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
